  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% accuracy while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is weak at 20.8%, making RNA the dominant modality and the primary target for improvement. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether the multiprofile structure (multiple profiles per cell) plus aggregation carries meaningful signal beyond a single profile. This experiment (config_002) isolates that question by changing only the profile setting from singleprofile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation, keeping the same pca_n2000 encoder as config_001. If accuracy improves, it confirms that profile structure matters and motivates testing transformer aggregation (config_003) and multiprofile with better encoders. If it does not improve, we learn that the bottleneck is encoder quality rather than profile structure, redirecting effort toward scvi/scgpt encoders. This is the most informative single-variable extension of our best result under a tight budget."
}

